{{Nihongo|'''Kazabune'''|傘船洲|Kazabune-shu}} is a country in Southwestern end of [[Lurandia]], bordering [[Kaneda]] in North, [[United Midlands]] in east. Kazabune is considered to be the westernmost part of Lurandia and the border between western and eastern hemisphere. 

Kazabune have its root on the decline of [[Umijin]] on [[Sanese Archipelago]] with [[Kurokoma clan]] exile considered to kickstart the sanese settlement on Kazabune. Over the time Kazabune settled by the exiles and the abducted people by the [[Sea Wolves]] over the coast of [[Kanemoto Shogunate]] during 13th century. With [[The Secret Trade]] influence, over the time Kazabune fosian demographic become more heterogenous in addition to Dagits, Zong and other people from [[Balausia Peninsula]] colonized Kazabune

It has a strong maritime cultures with the cross ocean trading and [[w:Whaling|Whaling]] being one of the main source of income until 19th century.

==Etymology==
The name Kazabune (傘船) consisted of 2 kanji, 傘 means umbrella and 船 means boats. The name itself considered to be the originated from the allegory of Kurokoma clan looking for the shades on their boat while venturing the Shendan Ocean from [[Nagashima (Nakamizu)|Nagashima]] in 1337. While the reading of kanji in standard sanese is Kasa-fune, the pronunciation of Kazabune believed to be drifted along the time with the mixture of language with native lurandians over the region

